---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import MascotSlot from "../components/MascotSlot.astro";
import BookCta from "../components/BookCta.astro";
import { personJsonLd, resume } from "../lib/resume";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Track Record · Josh Robinson, AI Consultant"
      description="20+ years building software and 2+ years running AI in production. BLDX, American Red Cross, Aetna, Bloomberg, a US patent, open source, and a book."
      jsonLd={personJsonLd(resume)}
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
      <header class="credentials hairline-grid">
        <MascotSlot
          slotId="S07"
          pose="walking forward, purposeful"
          src="/hexorx/hexorx-S07-walk.webp"
          assetWidth={600}
          assetHeight={760}
          desktopWidth={150}
          desktopHeight={190}
          mobileWidth={110}
          mobileHeight={150}
          bottomAligned
          alt="hexorx S07: walking forward, purposeful; final art pending"
        />
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">git log --career</p>
          <h1>Track record</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            A résumé, written for the people who might hire me. Here's what I've
            built, where I built it, and what each one means for your business.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="summary-strip">
        <div>
          <strong>20+ years</strong> building software, mostly as a founder or
          CTO.
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>2+ years</strong> running AI features in production with real
          users.
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Big and small:</strong> startups I co-founded, plus the
          American Red Cross, Aetna, and Bloomberg.
        </div>
      </div>

      <article class="role entry current">
        <header>
          <p class="mono">HEAD · BLDX · CTO and co-founder · 2021 to present</p>
          <p class="status">● current</p>
        </header>
        <h2>What I do</h2>
        <p>
          BLDX is an AI early-warning and continuous underwriting platform for
          buildings and construction projects. In plain terms, it reads the
          records a project produces, such as inspections, maintenance tickets,
          permits, contracts, and compliance documents, and flags risk before it
          turns into an insurance claim. People can also ask questions about
          those records in plain English.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            I set the technical direction from the company's founding and lead a
            small engineering team.
          </li>
          <li>
            Our AI features have been in production with real users for more
            than two years.
          </li>
          <li>
            I build with several AI providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, xAI, and
            Mistral) using LangChain and the Vercel AI SDK, so we can use the
            right model for each job.
          </li>
          <li>
            I measure AI quality with benchmarks, user feedback, and LangSmith,
            a tool for tracking and testing how AI performs.
          </li>
          <li>
            I work directly with insurance, facility management, compliance, and
            construction experts to turn how they work and what they know into
            AI workflows.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <h3>What it means for you</h3>
        <p>
          I've done the hard part already: taking AI past the demo and into
          daily use by real people, then keeping it accurate. I know how to sit
          with experts who aren't technical, learn their work, and build
          something they trust.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="role entry current">
        <header>
          <p class="mono">
            consulting · Independent technology consulting · 2018 to present
          </p>
          <p class="status">● ongoing</p>
        </header>
        <h2>What I do</h2>
        <p>
          Alongside my startup work, I've advised organizations on their
          technology, architecture, and engineering practice, and recommended
          practical build plans that fit small teams.
        </p>
        <h3>What it means for you</h3>
        <p>
          "Fits a small team" is the whole point. I'm used to recommending what
          a business can actually run and maintain, not the biggest possible
          system.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="role entry">
        <header>
          <p class="mono">
            main · American Red Cross · UI Architect · 2015 to 2018
          </p>
          <p class="status">○ past</p>
        </header>
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>
          I built the Red Cross's online donation forms. Every online donation
          made on the site ran through code I wrote. I also built a living style
          guide, a shared library of page components that product owners used to
          test options and pick what went into each new donation campaign. I
          worked closely with product managers and senior leadership to keep
          improving the donation experience.
        </p>
        <h3>What it means for you</h3>
        <p>
          I've built software that a large, mission-driven organization relied
          on for something that really mattered. And I built it so non-technical
          people could make their own choices without waiting on a developer.
          That's the same goal I have for the AI tools I set up for you.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="role entry">
        <header>
          <p class="mono">v5 · YouBase · Co-founder and CTO · 2016 to 2023</p>
          <p class="status">○ past</p>
        </header>
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>
          I led engineering on secure data systems for life sciences and
          healthcare, working with industry stakeholders so the systems met
          their standards and data-handling requirements.
        </p>
        <h3>What it means for you</h3>
        <p>
          When your business handles sensitive information, security and privacy
          aren't add-ons. I've designed for them from the start.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="role entry">
        <header>
          <p class="mono">tag · BitBoss · Co-founder · 2015 to 2020</p>
          <p class="status">◆ patented</p>
        </header>
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>
          I led teams building systems for real-money gaming, including mobile
          apps and the systems behind them. I'm the inventor on US Patent
          10,373,426, "System and Method for Provably Fair Gaming," granted in
          2019.
        </p>
        <h3>What it means for you</h3>
        <p>
          I've built systems where accuracy and trust weren't optional, and
          invented something new enough to patent.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="role entry">
        <header>
          <p class="mono">
            v4 · Aetna / iTriage · Web and Server Platform Architect · 2013 to
            2014
          </p>
          <p class="status">○ past</p>
        </header>
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>
          Platform architecture for iTriage, a consumer health product inside a
          major healthcare company.
        </p>
        <h3>What it means for you</h3>
        <p>
          I know how to work inside a large, regulated organization, with its
          processes, reviews, and stakeholders, and still ship.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="role entry">
        <header>
          <p class="mono">
            v3 · Bloomberg · Ruby on Rails Developer · 2012 to 2013
          </p>
          <p class="status">○ past</p>
        </header>
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>
          I worked on processing and indexing large data sets and improving
          system performance.
        </p>
        <h3>What it means for you</h3>
        <p>
          A lot of AI work is really data work: getting information organized
          and findable. I've done that with large data sets at Bloomberg.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="role entry">
        <header>
          <p class="mono">v2 · ShortTermHousing · CTO · 2010 to 2012</p>
          <p class="status">○ past</p>
        </header>
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>Built the product from scratch and automated how it was deployed.</p>
        <h3>What it means for you</h3>
        <p>
          I can take an idea from a blank page to something running, without a
          big team.
        </p>
      </article>

      <section>
        <h2>Earlier</h2>
        <ul class="deliverables">
          <li>Principal Engineer, Aha! Labs, 2014 to 2015</li>
          <li>Senior Lead Developer, Teliax, 2006 to 2010</li>
          <li>
            Co-founder and advisor, CodeCraftsmen, 2017 to present (part-time):
            technical strategy, team management, and mentoring developers
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <p class="kicker">ls ./shipped</p>
        <h2>Things I've made and shared</h2>
        <ul class="deliverables">
          <li>
            <span class="mono">◆ patent</span>
            <strong>US Patent 10,373,426</strong>, System and Method for
            Provably Fair Gaming. Inventor, granted 2019.
            <a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US10373426B2/en">
              Google Patents
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="mono">● oss</span>
            <strong>
              The <code>countries</code> Ruby gem.
            </strong>{" "}
            I'm the original author. It's an open-source library for country,
            currency, and phone data that other developers build on. It now
            lives at
            <a href="https://github.com/countries/countries">
              github.com/countries/countries
            </a>
            .
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="mono">○ published</span>
            <strong>
              <em>Introducing Meteor</em>
            </strong>{" "}
            (Apress, 2015). Co-author, with Aaron Gray and David Titarenco. A
            book for developers on the Meteor web framework.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="mono">● community</span>
            <strong>Denver MongoDB Meetup.</strong> I ran it, bringing local
            developers together to learn from each other.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Why this matters for you:</strong> Writing a book and running
          a meetup are teaching jobs. Training your team is the same skill: take
          something technical and make it make sense.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <p class="kicker">// stack</p>
        <h2>Tools I work with</h2>
        <div class="stack-groups">
          <div>
            <h3>AI models and tools</h3>
            <ul class="chips">
              <li>OpenAI</li>
              <li>Anthropic</li>
              <li>xAI</li>
              <li>Mistral</li>
              <li>LangChain</li>
              <li>Vercel AI SDK</li>
              <li>LangSmith</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Data</h3>
            <ul class="chips">
              <li>PostgreSQL</li>
              <li>MongoDB</li>
              <li>MySQL</li>
              <li>data pipelines</li>
              <li>APIs and system integration</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Infrastructure</h3>
            <ul class="chips">
              <li>AWS</li>
              <li>Docker</li>
              <li>Kubernetes</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Languages</h3>
            <ul class="chips">
              <li>Python</li>
              <li>TypeScript</li>
              <li>JavaScript</li>
              <li>Ruby</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <BookCta heading="Want this experience working on your business?" />
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
<style>
  .role h2 {
    font-size: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  @media print {
    :global(span.mascot-slot[data-mascot-slot="S07"]) {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
